        "id": 149024,
        "name": "Bunston",
        "username": "Bunston",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bunston/{size}/1939_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-28T19:56:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a rather long game with Vital Strength of the Earth, but I got to a point where I finally managed to get the board under control. I didn't want to place my last two presence until I needed them, as the VSE sacred sites are so useful as forts.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Does that make sense? Basically, I didn't want to put them in spot A, only to realize two turns later they would have been more usefull in spot B.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I agree that you almost always want to place presence on the board, but just having the option to hold off would be nice.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:27:24.377Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
